d CAGR. The total return for the selected period is displayed directly above the panels.\"},perfCheckAvgPerYearTracklist:{title:\"Avg. per Year (CAGR)\",body:\"CAGR is the annualized equivalent of your return. Computed as Compound Annual Growth Rate (CAGR) from {start_date} to {end_date}.\",howToRead:\"CAGR smooths out good and bad years into one number. \\u26a0\\ufe0f Because your portfolio is only {period_days} days old, this annualized figure can be highly volatile and should be interpreted with caution.\"},perfCheckRewardRiskTracklist:{title:\"Reward / Risk (Calmar Ratio)\",body:\"Portfolio Calmar Ratio for {start_date} \\u2192 {end_date}: annualized return ({cagr_pct}) divided by maximum drawdown ({max_dd_pct}). Result: {calmar_ratio}.\",howToRead:\"Calmar Ratio compares annualized return with maximum drawdown. Higher values indicate stronger returns relative to the worst historical drawdown. \\u26a0\\ufe0f For portfolios younger than 1 year, the ratio can be highly unstable because the return is annualized.\"},perfCheckRiskTracklist:{title:\"Max. Drawdown\",body:\"Worst peak-to-trough decline for your portfolio during {start_date} \\u2192 {end_date}, and how long it took to recover.\",howToRead:\"Smaller drawdown and shorter recovery = lower risk. These two numbers together describe the full pain story.\"},perfCheckDurationTracklist:{title:\"Drawdown Duration\",body:\"Peak-to-Trough Time. It took {days} days for your portfolio to drop from its highest peak to the lowest trough during the maximum drawdown.\",howToRead:\"Measures the capitulation phase. Shorter = sudden crash. Longer = prolonged market bleed.\"},perfCheckMultipleTracklist:{title:\"Backtest Portfolio vs Index\",body:\"S&P 500 Total Return (dividends reinvested) over the same period ({start_date} \\u2192 {end_date}): {benchmark_total_pct}. Your portfolio's return is compared with the market to show relative performance.\",howToRead:\"A multiple above 1.0\\xd7 means your portfolio outperformed the index. Below 1.0\\xd7 means underperformance. Context only, not advice.\"},diversificationTracklist:{title:\"Diversification Score\",body:\"This score measures the portfolio's concentration risk based strictly on sector exposure. A higher score means a more evenly distributed portfolio across market sectors.\",riskScale:!0},tracklistInceptionDate:{title:\"Backtest Start Date\",body:\"The date your backtest period starts ({inception_date}) \\u2014 {duration_days} days ago. All return metrics (Reward, Avg. per Year, Drawdown, etc.) are measured from this date.\",howToRead:\"Earlier inception = longer track record. More data means the metrics are more reliable.\"},tracklistEquityValue:{title:\"Equity Value (USD)\",body:\"The current total market value of all open positions in your portfolio, expressed in US dollars. It reflects your portfolio's worth at today's prices.\",howToRead:\"Higher = your portfolio has grown. Lower = it has declined. Compare to your starting capital to measure progress.\"},tracklistTodayChange:{title:\"Today's Change\",body:\"How much your portfolio's equity value moved today compared to yesterday's closing value. Shown in USD or % depending on the toggle.\",howToRead:\"Positive (green) = portfolio gained today. Negative (red) = it lost value. This is a single-day move, not the total return.\"},tracklistCashBalance:{title:\"Cash Balance\",body:\"The uninvested cash remaining in your portfolio after all buy and sell trades. This is the portion of your starting capital not currently deployed in open positions.\",howToRead:\"Higher cash = more of your capital is on the sideline. Lower cash = more is invested. Neither is inherently better.\"},equityHistoryChart:{title:\"Equity History\",body:\"This chart shows your portfolio value over time, not a single stock price. Each point represents the total value \\u2014 or percentage return \\u2014 of your portfolio on that trading day.\",howToRead:\"Switch % / USD to change the view between percentage ret